      "role": "user",
      "content": "Here it is: \"Section 4.2: Price Adjustments. The Supplier reserves the right to implement a seasonal surcharge of up to 5% on the base fuel rate during peak demand months (June-August) to account for market volatility. Such adjustments shall be applied automatically to all scheduled deliveries within the specified period without requiring prior written consent from SwiftRoute.\" \n\nDoes that give them the right to spike our rates unexpectedly? I really need to know if this is going to mess with our budget stability.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
